### Exercise 15: RESTful API Test Requests

### 1. GET all articles
GET http://localhost:3000/articles

### 2. POST create a new article (from Word Docx sample)
POST http://localhost:3000/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Exploring the Hidden Gems of Paris",
    "text": "Paris is known for its iconic landmarks like the Eiffel Tower and Louvre, but the city hides some lesser-known treasures. In this article, we'll explore some hidden gems of Paris that offer unique experiences away from the tourist crowds. From charming cafes tucked away in quiet lanes to serene gardens, Paris is full of surprises waiting to be discovered.",
    "comments": [
        {
            "body": "Absolutely love this guide! Can't wait to explore these places.",
            "date": "2023-06-03"
        },
        {
            "body": "Paris is always full of surprises. Great article!",
            "date": "2023-06-04"
        }
    ],
    "tags": ["Paris", "Travel", "Guide"]
}

### 3. PUT on /articles (Should return 403 Forbidden)
PUT http://localhost:3000/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Cannot update all articles"
}

### 4. GET article by ID (replace <ID> with actual _id from response above)
GET http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>

### 5. PUT update article by ID
PUT http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Long News"
}

### 6. POST on /articles/:id (Should return 403 Forbidden)
POST http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Cannot post with ID"
}

### 7. DELETE article by ID
DELETE http://localhost:3000/articles/<REPLACE_WITH_ARTICLE_ID>

### 8. DELETE all articles
DELETE http://localhost:3000/articles
